Search for a spiralled INVITE's dialog with no direction set.

dlg_new_dialog() passes &dir to search_dlg() to detect a spiral - the
same INVITE coming back through this CSCF - but dir is not initialised
until after the search. match_dialog() reads it to pick what to compare
while the dialog has no dlg_out entries yet:

	DLG_DIR_DOWNSTREAM (1)	from_tag against the From tag
	DLG_DIR_UPSTREAM (2)	from_tag against the To tag
	anything else		both, and sets *dir to the one that matched

With stack garbage of 2 a spiralled INVITE, which has no To tag, is
compared on the wrong tag, no spiral is detected and a second dialog is
created for the same Call-ID. Seen under valgrind memcheck on the P-CSCF
and the S-CSCF ("Conditional jump or move depends on uninitialised
value(s)" at match_dialog, origin the stack frame of dlg_new_dialog).

dlg_onroute() and dlg_get_msg_dialog() set DLG_DIR_NONE before their
lookups; do the same here.

diff --git a/src/modules/ims_dialog/dlg_handlers.c b/src/modules/ims_dialog/dlg_handlers.c
index d14e5e039c..ff40a2b3a4 100644
--- a/src/modules/ims_dialog/dlg_handlers.c
+++ b/src/modules/ims_dialog/dlg_handlers.c
@@ -1680,7 +1680,7 @@ int dlg_new_dialog(
 	str ftag;
 	str ttag;
 	str req_uri;
-	unsigned int dir;
+	unsigned int dir = DLG_DIR_NONE;
 	int mlock;
 
 	if(req->first_line.u.request.method_value != METHOD_INVITE)
